From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:53:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: reserve crash-log RAM on ThinkSmart View

The kernel enables pstore, but without a reserved RAM backend no kernel
logs survive a reset. Reserve 1 MiB outside the firmware and framebuffer
carveouts for panic records, the kernel console and userspace messages.
Use ECC to help recover records after an unclean warm reset.

Source: local device integration, not an upstream backport.
Base: msm8953-mainline/linux 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429,
with this device's preceding kernel patches applied.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index a3674f565..be5b671a3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -142,6 +142,16 @@
 	reserved-memory {
 		/* part of modem node removal */
 		/delete-node/ rmtfs@f2d00000;
 
+		ramoops@9ff00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x9ff00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		cont_splash_mem: cont-splash@90001000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x90001000 0x0 (800 * 1280 * 3)>;
-- 
2.56.1

